invalid.js:2:27 lint/nursery/useExpectToHaveBeenCalledTimes  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i toHaveLength() is used to check how many times a mock function was called.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ expect(method.mock.calls).toHaveLength(1);
      │                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ expect(method.mock.calls).toHaveLength(0);
    4 │ expect(method.mock.calls).toHaveLength(count);
  
  i When this check fails, the error message describes the length of an array instead of the number of calls.
  
  i Use toHaveBeenCalledTimes() to check the number of calls.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Use toHaveBeenCalledTimes() instead.
  
     1  1 │   /* should generate diagnostics */
     2    │ - expect(method.mock.calls).toHaveLength(1);
        2 │ + expect(method).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
     3  3 │   expect(method.mock.calls).toHaveLength(0);
     4  4 │   expect(method.mock.calls).toHaveLength(count);
  

